  m_Name: 1_Definition
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Title: Definition
  Description: 'An analgesic or painkiller is any member of the group of drugs used
    to achieve analgesia, relief from pain. Analgesic drugs act in various ways on
    the peripheral and central nervous systems. They are distinct from anaesthetics,
    which temporarily affect, and in some instances completely eliminate, sensation. '
